  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Union Cabinet has moved forward with an amended Delimitation Bill, intended to increase the number of parliamentary seats from 543 to 806. The revised legislation includes a population freeze until 2051 and seeks to address previous legal concerns regarding the process. Prime Minister Narendra Modi expressed that the bill aligns with the government's Nari Shakti initiatives. However, the proposal has caused significant internal friction within the INDIA opposition bloc. While the DMK and the NCP (SP) faction have announced their support for the measure, citing consistency with their regional objectives and party positions, other opposition leaders remain critical. Some critics, including representatives from the Congress party and other alliance partners, have labeled the bill as a threat to electoral rights and have called for a united legislative front to oppose its passage in the upcoming special session of Parliament.",
